From aae62ac0afa056bba5d465d68ccac56bfe8d8139 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Marcelo Poblete (via Claude)" <marcelopoblete.us@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 17:32:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: relocate map basemap/layers/zoom controls into
 right-edge icon toolbar (AXIS-style)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Replace the always-visible basemap switcher and fiber-layers/coverage
  checkbox panel with a vertical icon dock docked to the right edge of
  the map, matching the AXIS Site Designer reference UI.
- Clicking the stacked-layers icon toggles a flyout containing the
  Basemap segmented control, Fiber Layers checkboxes, and Coverage
  (FOV/DORI/Night IR) checkboxes — same state/logic, new container.
- Add Zoom In / Zoom Out buttons directly in the icon dock.
- Remove the now-duplicated 'Fit to elements' button from the
  top-left toolbar (kept only in the new right-side dock).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ScqTACWd5u51GDZPenDDdM
